  "preamble": "Nasalization of the bilabial implosive: [ɓ] becomes the nasal [m]. In Vietnamese, Proto-Vietic *ɓ regularly gives m (muối 'salt', mấy 'how many', mướp 'loofah'), and also in mắc, mủ and măng, while conservative Vietic languages such as Kri, Chứt and Arem keep a b-like stop. Independently, in the Southwestern Tai languages Shan and Tai Nüa, Proto-Tai *ɓ (Li's *ʔb) became m, whereas Thai and Lao keep b (Proto-Tai *ɓaɰᴬ 'leaf' > Thai ใบ bai, Shan မႂ်, Tai Nüa ᥛᥬ /maɯ/). Ahom shows both b- and m- spellings.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Nasalization, Airstream Change",
